### CrateDB version

5.10.3

### CrateDB setup information

Single node

### Problem description

In some cases it makes sense to use different analyzers for indexing and search.
See for instance the Apple/appli example at https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/analysis-index-search-time.html

Trying to do this with CrateDB seems to lead to either a SQLParseException or unexpected results.
See repro steps below.

### Steps to Reproduce

In the steps below we always insert the string lowercase and try to match with a search expression in uppercase.

In the first block, we index with the `letter` tokenizer and search with the same one, there is no match, which is expected.

In the second block, we index with the `lowercase` tokenizer and search with the same one, there is a match which is also expected.

In the 3rd block, we use the index with the `lowercase` tokenizer and attempt to search with the `letter` tokenizer, no match is expected, but instead we get a `SQLParseException`.

In the 4th block, we have `ix1` with the lowercase tokenizer and `ix2` with the `letter` tokenizer, we attempt to search with the `letter` tokenizer against `ix1`, no match is expected, but instead one math is found as it would have used the `lowercase` tokenizer for search.

```sql
CREATE ANALYZER my_analyzer_letter ( TOKENIZER "letter");
CREATE ANALYZER my_analyzer_lowercase ( TOKENIZER "lowercase");

CREATE TABLE test_fts (
	txt TEXT,
	INDEX ix1 USING fulltext (txt) WITH (analyzer='my_analyzer_letter')
);

INSERT INTO test_fts VALUES ('test');
REFRESH TABLE test_fts;

SELECT txt,_score
FROM test_fts 
WHERE MATCH(ix1, 'TEST') USING phrase WITH (analyzer='my_analyzer_letter');
--> Search TEST against test --> 0 rows - good 

DROP TABLE test_fts;

CREATE TABLE test_fts (
	txt TEXT,
	INDEX ix1 USING fulltext (txt) WITH (analyzer='my_analyzer_lowercase')
);

INSERT INTO test_fts VALUES ('test');
REFRESH TABLE test_fts;

SELECT txt,_score
FROM test_fts 
WHERE MATCH(ix1, 'TEST') USING phrase WITH (analyzer='my_analyzer_lowercase');
--> Search test against test 
--> 1 row good

SELECT txt,_score
FROM test_fts 
WHERE MATCH(ix1, 'TEST') USING phrase WITH (analyzer='my_analyzer_letter');
--> should search TEST again test
--> SQLParseException[No analyzer found for [my_analyzer_letter]]

DROP TABLE test_fts;

CREATE TABLE test_fts (
	txt TEXT,
	INDEX ix1 USING fulltext (txt) WITH (analyzer='my_analyzer_lowercase'),
	INDEX ix2 USING fulltext (txt) WITH (analyzer='my_analyzer_letter')
);

INSERT INTO test_fts VALUES ('test');
REFRESH TABLE test_fts;

SELECT txt,_score
FROM test_fts 
WHERE MATCH(ix1, 'TEST') USING phrase WITH (analyzer='my_analyzer_letter');
--> should search TEST again test but seems to search test against test
--> 1 row ? 
```

### Actual Result

`SQLParseException` / search with the tokenizer of the index

### Expected Result

Search with the tokenizer specified in the match

