issue_body:
### CrateDB version

5.9.3

### CrateDB setup information

Any number of crate nodes and with 8GB+ memory.

### Problem description

When we execute a query using a prepared statement, it returns duplicate records, while running the same query directly on the CrateDB console gives the correct results.

Note: this issue is reproduced in CrateDB version - 5.1.0 also

### Steps to Reproduce

This issue can be reproduced using [this data](https://community.cratedb.com/t/in-clause-on-primary-key-column-does-not-return-all-the-records-if-it-has-more-than-5k-inputs/1878/3)

```
String query = "select * from uu.records where  rday=?  AND  ( ( id  IN  ('161070') AND recordid=? )  OR  ( id  IN  ('161070') AND recordid=? ) )";
Connection con = null;
PreparedStatement ps = null;
ResultSet rs = null;

try{
      List<Object> ids = new ArrayList<>();
      con = getCrateConnection();
      ps = con.prepareStatement(query);

      ps.setLong(1, 1727375400000L);
      ps.setLong(2, 110);
      ps.setLong(3, 110);

      rs = ps.executeQuery();

       while(rs.next()){
                ids.add(rs.getString(1));
        }
            System.out.println("Number of records: " + ids.size());

        }catch (Exception e){
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
```


### Actual Result

 It returns duplicate records ( 2 records ).

### Expected Result

It should return single record.

