issue_body:
I'd like to report a regression with NullAway 0.12.8.

NullAway 0.12.8 will report a false positive, reporting that `be` should be checked for `case null`, however due to the `instanceof` check, there is no possibility of it being `null`.

NullAway 0.12.7 will not report the false positive.

```java
private static Throwable throwableToProto(Throwable t) {
        if (!(t instanceof RuntimeException rte) || !(rte.getCause() instanceof BusinessException be)) {
            return t;
        }

        return switch (be) {
            case BusinessExceptionUnauthenticated e -> UNAUTHENTICATED
                    .withDescription(e.getMessage())
                    .asRuntimeException();
            case BusinessExceptionNotFound e -> NOT_FOUND
                    .withDescription(e.getMessage())
                    .asRuntimeException();
            default -> Status.UNKNOWN
                    .withDescription(be.getMessage())
                    .asRuntimeException();
        };
    }
```

