issue_body:
### Redis version

8.0

### Redisson version

3.50.0

### Redisson configuration

Default docker image configuration.

### What is the Expected behavior?

When using `tryAcquire` on `RPermitExpirableSemaphore` with > 1 permits. The thread is notified when the permits has been released and acquires them before end of the `waitTime`.

### What is the Actual behavior?

`tryAcquire` on `RPermitExpirableSemaphore` with > 1 permits when not able to acquire the permits on the first attempt it waints untill `waitTime` ends even though other thread has already released the permits.

### Additional information

At first glance the thread hangs on 
https://github.com/redisson/redisson/blob/5ec8ffca89d45ecdef3d24ed2d48268153f3b267/redisson/src/main/java/org/redisson/RedissonPermitExpirableSemaphore.java#L99
because it tries to acquire > 1 permit, but 
https://github.com/redisson/redisson/blob/5ec8ffca89d45ecdef3d24ed2d48268153f3b267/redisson/src/main/java/org/redisson/pubsub/SemaphorePubSub.java#L42
releases only 1 permit (counter is 1 as only 1 thread was waiting).

Check the following test which should not be failing when the bug is resolved.

```

@Slf4j
public class TestE2ETest extends AbstractE2ETest {

    @Autowired
    private RedissonClient redissonClient;

    @Test
    void test() throws InterruptedException {
        String semaphoreName = "sem-name";
        int permits = 2;

        AtomicBoolean result = new AtomicBoolean(false);
        var t1 = new Thread(() -> {
            List<String> permitList = this.lockSemaphore(semaphoreName, permits, true);

            try {
                Thread.sleep(5_000);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                throw new RuntimeException(e);
            }

            this.unlockSemaphore(semaphoreName, permitList);

        });

        var t2 = new Thread(() -> {
            List<String> permitList = this.lockSemaphore(semaphoreName, permits, false);

            result.set(true);

            this.unlockSemaphore(semaphoreName, permitList);
        });

        t1.start();
        Thread.sleep(1_000);
        t2.start();

        t1.join();
        t2.join();

        assertThat(result.get()).isTrue();
    }

    public List<String> lockSemaphore(String semaphoreName, int permits, boolean init) {
        RPermitExpirableSemaphore semaphore = this.redissonClient.getPermitExpirableSemaphore(semaphoreName);

        try {
            if (init) {
                semaphore.trySetPermits(permits);
            }

            List<String> permitIds = semaphore.tryAcquire(permits, 5_000, -1, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);

            if (permitIds.size() != permits) {
                throw new RuntimeException("Unable to acquire semaphore permits");
            }
            return permitIds;
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Interrupted while waiting for semaphore permits", e);
        }
    }

    public void unlockSemaphore(String semaphoreName, List<String> permits) {
        RPermitExpirableSemaphore semaphore = this.redissonClient.getPermitExpirableSemaphore(semaphoreName);
        semaphore.tryRelease(permits);
    }
}

